The change caches the result of `GetType()` in a local variable. The original code calls it up to twice per invocation. In the SDK it is a virtual call, so the compiler cannot merge the two calls.

This assumes `GetType()` has no side effects, as in the SDK. Under that assumption the behavior is unchanged.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 FieldBase::GetNumValues(void) const
{
    if (!IsValid())
        return 0;

    const FIT_UINT8 type = GetType();

    if (type != FIT_BASE_TYPE_STRING)
        return (FIT_UINT8)(values.size() / baseTypeSizes[type & FIT_BASE_TYPE_NUM_MASK]);

    return (FIT_UINT8)stringIndexes.size();
}
```